WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.631
Hi, I'm Davit!

00:00:02.631 --> 00:00:05.396
Block says Dessa learned to talk from audio alone.

00:00:05.396 --> 00:00:07.853
Here's how a model like that takes turns.

00:00:09.433 --> 00:00:11.570
The idea: listen and speak on one clock.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.775
Every tick, read a frame of you, write a frame of itself.

00:00:18.983 --> 00:00:22.966
A cascade waits for you to stop, transcribes, and reads an answer back.

00:00:22.966 --> 00:00:24.805
The laugh never reaches the model.

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:28.686
A full-duplex model never stops listening, so a quick yeah while you

00:00:28.686 --> 00:00:30.705
talk is just a likely next frame.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.661
A codec turns each slice of your audio into a few tokens.

00:00:36.081 --> 00:00:38.705
Your tokens and the model's own sit side by side.

00:00:39.281 --> 00:00:41.951
A transformer trained on recorded calls reads it all.

00:00:42.481 --> 00:00:46.454
It writes its next frame, speech or silence, and feeds it back.

00:00:46.454 --> 00:00:47.778
Listening is predicting silence.

00:00:49.775 --> 00:00:53.028
Moshi, the open reference design, leans on a text model.

00:00:53.028 --> 00:00:54.654
Block says Dessa drops it.

00:00:55.074 --> 00:00:56.372
No text tokens at all.

00:00:57.561 --> 00:00:58.738
No pretrained model.

00:00:58.738 --> 00:01:00.701
Trained from scratch on conversation.

00:01:01.121 --> 00:01:02.399
One rack of GPUs.

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:03.996
No paper or weights yet.

00:01:05.717 --> 00:01:08.925
Block did publish demo calls, each speaker on its own track.

00:01:09.345 --> 00:01:11.207
So you can time exactly who talks when.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:16.807
Dessa's median gap before it starts talking is about a quarter of a second.

00:01:16.807 --> 00:01:18.935
Its human partners wait a little longer.

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:23.287
And it starts in overlap slightly more often than they do.

00:01:26.017 --> 00:01:28.188
Timing can be learned from sound alone.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:31.289
Facts, failure rates and a fair test are still missing.

00:01:33.983 --> 00:01:38.415
One clock, two streams, no text, and human timing in the demos Block chose.

00:01:38.835 --> 00:01:40.971
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:40.971 --> 00:01:41.581
I'm Davit.

00:01:41.581 --> 00:01:41.886
Bye!
